 "_comment": "Primary source of support for research doctorate recipients, by citizenship, across seven SED releases. Percentages are of each citizenship group, not of the total. The RESEARCH ASSISTANTSHIP row is the closest published proxy for federal funding -- GSS shows federal support reaches doctoral students overwhelmingly through RAs -- but it is a proxy: the SED does not record which award paid. The series runs on ALL FIELDS because NCSES revised the field taxonomy in the 2023 release, so an S&E series would cross a definitional break; the S&E rollup is carried only where the release publishes it.",
